return {
  summary = "Log in, get a Trainer ID, add friends in-game, and see their last-known positions - async, plain-HTTP presence, no server process required (Android-friendly).",
  author = "Ash",
  tags = { "multiplayer", "online", "overworld", "presence" },
  differences = {
    added = {
      "Trainer ID: a unique 5-digit id (00000-65535, same range as the mainline games) assigned once at registration and shown on the status screen - the key used to add friends in-game.",
      "In-game Add Friend screen: a D-pad digit spinner (UP/DOWN changes a digit, LEFT/RIGHT moves the cursor, A sends the request) - no typing, no web page, just enter a friend's Trainer ID.",
      "Incoming friend requests: polled on the same ~30s cycle as presence, shown as a REQUESTS count on the status screen, paged through and accepted on their own screen (LEFT from the status screen).",
      "GitHub auto-update: manifest.json now sets \"github\" so the launcher's Update / Other Versions can pull new releases directly - see .github/workflows/release-silphnet.yml (packages only mod/silphnet/, never the server source or docs, as a GitHub Release .zip on every push to main that touches the mod).",
      "Friend markers show their name: press A on a friend's map marker to see who it is, in a small text box that closes on A or B - a live lookup done at the moment you press A, not baked in when the marker appeared.",
      "Friends list now shows each friend's Trainer ID, and a LEFT/RIGHT:PAGE hint when you have more than one friend.",
      "Global online count: shown on the status screen's FRIENDS line (\"FRIENDSn ONn\") - everyone currently online, not just friends.",
      "NEARBY: a second Start Menu row (\"SN NEARBY\") opens its own screen showing everyone else currently on your own map, by name and Trainer ID, titled with how many people are there and the map name - Pokemon-Go-style. Shows ALREADY A FRIEND for someone you've added, or NOT YET A FRIEND with a reminder to add them the normal way (RIGHT from the SilphNet status screen) using the Trainer ID shown.",
      "Friend detail screen: press A on a friend in the friends list to see their self-reported stats (badges, Pokedex seen/caught, League wins, money) and latest activity - a real, event-driven catch message on two lines (\"CAUGHT LVL 25\" / \"BLASTOISE\") with its own time-ago, plus last-seen repeated from the main friends list. Stats upload on a slower ~3 min cycle than presence; activity uploads immediately on the real pokemon.caught event, not a poll. Badge count is derived from save.inventory checked against the constants.badges registry (Badges.count() itself isn't mod-accessible) - a faithful reimplementation of the engine's own internal logic, confirmed against its real source rather than guessed.",
      "Real game version detection: game.save.version (\"red\"/\"blue\"/\"yellow\"/\"gold\", confirmed directly from SaveData.lua's own save-table construction, guaranteed non-nil by an engine migration) now populates gameVersion, replacing the permanent \"UNKNOWN\" placeholder that had sat unverified since early in the project. The friends list shows an online friend's current version on the page-counter line (\"1/3 (BLUE)\", hidden while offline); the friend detail screen shows every version with real data as its own set of pages in one flat A-press cycle (see below).",
      "Time Played on the friend detail STATS page (\"TIME 34H 12M\") - reads game.save.playTime, which has two possible shapes engine-side (a plain seconds count, or an {hours,minutes,seconds,frames} table), normalized client-side into one total-seconds value before upload.",
      "Party page on the friend detail screen: cycle to PARTY (via A, alongside STATS/ACTIVITY) to see a friend's party, one mon per screen (species, level, current/max HP, up to 4 moves), paged with LEFT/RIGHT. No sprite - the mod API has no documented way to draw a species sprite outside the overworld NPC marker system, only text, so this stays text-only like every other screen. Encoded client-side as one compact delimited string (not JSON) and stored in a new friend_stats.party column, following this project's existing \"no JSON library available\" convention.",
    },
    changed = {
      "Status screen controls swapped once logged in: A now opens the friends list (was START), START is now re-auth (was A's secondary job). Pre-login, A still retries login / confirms account creation exactly as before - only the post-login bindings changed.",
      "Start Menu labels shortened from \"SILPHNET\" to \"SN\" (e.g. \"SN ASHJAM\", \"SN NEARBY\", \"SN SET NAME/PASS\") - some third-party UI mods truncate long Start Menu rows by chopping off anything past a length limit rather than adding an ellipsis, so a longer label could disappear entirely depending on name length. The full-screen status title (\"- SILPHNET -\") is unchanged since that's a roomier context.",
      "Friends list: A now opens the new friend detail screen instead of paging to the next friend - paging moved to DPAD LEFT/RIGHT only (SELECT:REMOVE is unchanged), same convention the Nearby screen already used.",
      "Friend detail screen redesigned: A is now the ONLY navigation button, cycling in one flat loop through every version's STATS page, then that version's ACTIVITY page, then the next version's STATS/ACTIVITY, wrapping back to the start - replacing an interim two-axis LEFT/RIGHT-for-page-type plus SELECT-for-version scheme this same version briefly shipped with internally before this correction. A version only gets pages in the cycle if it has real stats or activity data - presence-only versions (pinged but never reported stats) don't appear. The game version is now shown on its own line under the page title (\"ARCHADA STATS\" / \"BLUE\") for every friend, not just multi-version ones.",
    },
    fixed = {
      "About Silphnet no longer closes the Start Menu/options screen entirely when selected. It used to live as an \"ABOUT SILPHNET\" row on the mod manager's own OPTIONS screen, pushing the in-game SilphNetAbout screen from there - that push didn't behave the way the same push does from the Start Menu, and selecting it just closed the menu instead of opening About. Moved to its own \"SN ABOUT\" Start Menu row instead, the same already-working push site SN ASHJAM/SN NEARBY use. The About screen itself now also shows GitHub (ASHJAMB), Instagram (@ASHJAMGRAM), and TikTok (@ASHJAM) alongside the existing name/site/thanks/version - no Discord row yet, added once one exists.",
      "Start Menu label could go stale: if login finished while the player was standing still at boot (before any world.stepped event drained the HTTP result), the \"SN ...\" row wouldn't update to \"SN <name>\" until something else happened to drain the result first - e.g. opening and leaving the status screen. The Start Menu hook now drains pending HTTP results itself before computing the label, so the very first menu open after a completed login already shows the right name.",
      "Old UNKNOWN game_version rows no longer get orphaned once a player updates to this version. game_version is part of the primary key on presence/friend_stats/friend_activity, so a plain upsert keyed on the newly-detected real version couldn't touch the old UNKNOWN row - it would insert a SECOND row instead, leaving the first behind as dead data forever. ping.php now re-keys an account's existing UNKNOWN row onto the real version the moment it's known (once per account, automatically, on that account's next ping after updating) - no manual database cleanup needed. See migrations.sql for the full explanation and how to check progress.",
      "Friends list bottom rows no longer look squashed. Moving the friend N/M counter onto the title line (alongside \"FRIENDS\" - \"FRIENDS 1/3\") freed exactly one 8px row that used to be its own separate line; that row is now used as real clearance between the last data line (\"N HR AGO\") and the hint block below, which is what was actually reported as squashed - not the name/ID/status rows, which keep their original spacing. A:DETAIL and LEFT/RIGHT:PAGE are now combined onto one hint line (\"A:DETAIL LR:PAGE\") since this screen was already at its 144px display limit with 3 separate hint lines and had no other row to spare for the fix. The online version tag (introduced in 1.6.0) moved off the title line onto the ONLINE/OFFLINE line itself (\"ONLINE (BLUE)\") - reads more naturally there, and left enough room on the title line to restore the \"FRIENDS\" text once the version tag no longer needed the space.",
      "Status screen's A:FRIENDS hint no longer shows a placeholder online count. It used to always show something in brackets - \"(- ON)\" before the first online-count fetch landed, or \"(0 ON)\" once it landed with nobody online - which read as a stuck feature rather than a real indicator. The \"(N ON)\" suffix is now dropped entirely whenever there's nobody online, appearing only once there's a genuine positive count to report.",
    },
    known = {
      "Marker sprite is fixed to SPRITE_RED for now",
      "No battles, trades or chat - presence and friends only",
      "GitHub auto-update requires the repo to be reachable by the launcher (e.g. public, or however Gen1Recomp's manager handles private-repo auth) - not verified on-device yet",
      "Only 8 friend markers can be identified (pressed on for their name) at once on the same map - plenty for normal use, but raise MARKER_SLOTS in main.lua if ever needed",
      "Friend stats/activity are self-reported: a mod can only ever read its OWN game.save, so a friend's stats only show up once THEIR client has actually uploaded a snapshot - a brand new friend, or one who hasn't been online since updating to this version, shows NO STATS YET until their own client catches up.",
      "Activity currently only reports catches (real pokemon.caught event, with level from the event's own mon payload) - trainer-battle events (\"DFTD BUG CATCHER\" etc.) aren't wired up: the engine's documented events don't cleanly support this yet (world.trainer_engaged has the trainer's class but fires at battle START with no outcome; battle.ended has a result but no trainer identity) - would need to stitch the two together and hasn't been tested. Level-up/badge-earned/League-win aren't wired up either, though the same upload path (stats.php's activity field) would support them.",
    },
  },
  credits = {
    { who = "Ash Brittain (AshJam)", for_ = "SilphNet - concept, code, and server (ash.jamtv.co.uk)" },
    { who = "bryanthaboi", for_ = "Gen1Recomp engine and its mod platform" },
    { who = "Gamecorner33 & alamops", for_ = "Gen1Online / RBY MMO - prior art for the concept" },
  },
  compat = { modApi = 2 },
}
